{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-149510",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number obtained by spinning the spinner. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{2,3,…,9\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =9-2+1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{2,3,…,9\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{8}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{63}{12}=5.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the numbers obtained is $5.25$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
